Z||000000||Kerry Lacy||08-31-2001||09:39 PM||||I have an 86 SE V6 with auto transmission and when the engine is cold the idle will hunt and the engine will sometimes die.  After the engine warms up this problem goes away, almost .  The hunting idle will only flutuate 200 rpm's or so.  This only happens when in park.  When in drive or reverse no problem.  I have checked everything and can not solve this one.  Someone told me it might be th parl/neutral switch so I changed it out.  No help.  Do you think it may be in the conector or the wiring from the switch?  I was also told that this switch controls the IAC valve when in park or neutral by send a certain amount of voltage to the ECM to control the IAC.  The idle hunts from 900 rpm's to 1400 rpms when cold and in park.  Anyone have any advice on this one?  I'm out of ideas and not sure what to look for now.||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||09-01-2001||02:23 AM||||This is a very common "problem" w/ Fieros. Alot of them do it, even some of mine do it, but only for a minute or so...not that big of a deal really, its not gonna hurt anything. <BR>If you want to fix it though, use the search function on here...there have been lots of posts about this topic. Good luck, and welcome to the forum. <P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||c m west||09-01-2001||02:25 AM||||if nothing else, pull out the IAC valve and clean the bore in the throttle body. Before re-installing the IAC valve, make sure the plunger is 1 and 1/8 of an inch from the bore - this will ensure that its counts are properly set and fully functional||||reg||1
